WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.583
Hi.

00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:03.750
Hi.

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:05.667
I've loved you
my whole life.

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:07.917
One way or another.

00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:14.792
Well, well, well.

00:00:15.375 --> 00:00:16.208
Prodigal son.

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:18.500
You're the prodigal one.

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:21.125
I'm just the black sheep.

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:22.042
Where were you?

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.500
In New York.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.000
Upstate New York.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:28.500
I guessed that.

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:32.875
I mean, when you...
ran away,

00:00:32.958 --> 00:00:35.000
it was a subject
of a lot of debate.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.125
Many people had theories

00:00:37.208 --> 00:00:39.000
and most of them
were Hollywood, but...

00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:41.917
that was one of my guesses.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.833
Why?

00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:45.000
Covered bridges...

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.208
-You remember that?
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:51.917
Told you that
like half our lives ago.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.333
Are you really walking by
without saying hi?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:56.833
Should get going,

00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.708
I don't want to keep
my parents waiting.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.958
Some things never change.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.833
I remember
a 15-year-old Riley

00:01:07.917 --> 00:01:09.625
sneaking out
of my bedroom window

00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:11.667
trying to make curfew.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.875
I did my fearless
moral inventory

00:01:17.542 --> 00:01:20.000
and I found out that...

00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.667
man, I'm a coward.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:24.458
Don't do that.

00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:27.250
Don't talk about yourself
like that.

00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:29.958
If anyone else
talked about you like that,

00:01:30.042 --> 00:01:30.875
I'd...

00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:33.417
What?

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.208
Kick their ass.

00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:41.542
-Oh, yeah?
-Yeah.

00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:42.958
-Kick their ass?
-I'd kick it.

00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:44.042
Just like this. Oh!

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.583
That was actually
my thigh, so...

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.208
-So I'd kick their thighs?
-Yeah.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.000
I have this, um...

00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:55.917
dream.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.667
This recurring dream
about it since I was inside.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.500
I'm floating out
in the middle of the bay,

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:06.167
in the middle of the waters.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.542
Grey water, morning water.

00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:10.417
And the more
I have that dream,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.417
the more I just know

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.000
that it's not
in the cards for me.

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.000
I'm not getting off
this island.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:18.500
I know it.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.333
And at night,

00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.417
no matter what I might
let myself hope or...

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.000
I know it.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.583
But you...

00:02:31.042 --> 00:02:32.000
you do anyway.

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:35.417
You always could
do anything.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.333
Hi.

00:02:43.292 --> 00:02:44.500
Hi.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.750
I had that dream again
last night.

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:49.375
The one on the water?

00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:51.708
Yeah. Just like always.

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:55.542
Waiting on the sun.
But this time...

00:03:04.167 --> 00:03:05.000
you're there too.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:09.000
What do you think
that means?

00:03:13.542 --> 00:03:16.333
You could come back
tonight, maybe.

00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:20.625
I can do that.

00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:29.333
Where the hell
have you been?

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:30.917
I have been calling you
all day!

00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:32.958
-I'm sorry.
-Don't do that.

00:03:33.042 --> 00:03:34.042
Where were you?

00:03:35.125 --> 00:03:35.958
Where were you?

00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:45.542
Do you remember a few days
before you left town?

00:03:46.708 --> 00:03:48.167
Crawled in my window,

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.000
woke me up,
scared the shit out of me.

00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:52.625
You wanted
to take a boat out,

00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:54.083
wouldn’t take no
for an answer,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.000
so we grabbed a row boat
and rowed out.

00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.042
Far.

00:03:58.833 --> 00:04:01.375
Smoked a pack of cigarettes,
watched the sun come up.

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:02.833
Will you do that
with me now...

00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:06.000
and go for a ride?

00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:10.375
So, you've told me
that story,

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:11.667
you...

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.167
brought me out here,

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.083
you...

00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:18.083
have brought us out here

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:21.875
where there is nowhere
for me to go.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.417
I brought you out here,
so I'd have nowhere to go.

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:33.000
I'm not as strong as you.

00:04:34.833 --> 00:04:35.667
I never was.

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:41.000
I knew you wouldn't believe
any of this unless you saw.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.583
I want you...

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:46.583
to run.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.958
But I believe
you're going to row back

00:04:50.042 --> 00:04:52.125
and do everything you can
to try save them.

00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:56.833
I'm just so sorry
you have to see this.

00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:04.042
I love you, Erin Greene.

00:05:07.458 --> 00:05:09.000
I've loved you
my whole life.

00:05:10.292 --> 00:05:11.250
One way or another...

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:14.458
I love you too.

00:05:16.542 --> 00:05:17.500
I did my best.

00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:20.167
I did my best.

00:05:56.958 --> 00:05:59.333
So, what do you think
happens when we die, Erin?

00:06:02.833 --> 00:06:04.208
Speaking for myself?

00:06:07.708 --> 00:06:09.875
The body stops,
a cell at a time,

00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:13.167
but the brain keeps firing
those neurons.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.583
Little lightning bolts
like fireworks inside

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:20.542
and I thought I'd despair
or feel afraid,

00:06:20.625 --> 00:06:22.250
but I don't feel
any of that.

00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:24.292
None of it.

00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:26.792
Because I'm too busy...

00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:29.750
too busy in this moment

00:06:30.708 --> 00:06:31.542
remembering.

00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:36.458
And of course...

00:06:37.583 --> 00:06:40.667
I remember
that every atom in my body

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.167
was forged in a star.

00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:46.583
This matter, this body,

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.958
is mostly
just empty space, after all,

00:06:49.042 --> 00:06:50.500
and solid matter,

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.250
it's just energy
vibrating very slowly

00:06:54.333 --> 00:06:55.792
and there is no me.

00:06:56.708 --> 00:06:57.667
There never was.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.875
The electrons of my body
mingle and dance

00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:04.917
with the electrons
of the ground below me

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.833
and the air.

00:07:05.917 --> 00:07:07.208
I'm longer breathing.

00:07:08.625 --> 00:07:09.625
And I remember...

00:07:11.417 --> 00:07:13.750
there is no point
where any of that ends

00:07:14.708 --> 00:07:16.000
and I begin.

00:07:17.458 --> 00:07:21.000
We are the cosmos
dreaming of itself.

00:07:22.042 --> 00:07:25.000
It's simply a dream
that I think is my life.

00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:25.917
Every time.

00:07:28.042 --> 00:07:29.000
But I'll forget this,

00:07:29.958 --> 00:07:30.792
I always do.

00:07:32.292 --> 00:07:34.000
I always forget my dreams.

